# Team

Nexy is maintained by a small core team and supported by community contributors.

## Core maintainers

- **Anomaly** — creator and lead maintainer. Responsible for project direction, architecture decisions, and final review of all major changes.

## Maintainers

We are looking for additional maintainers. If you have made substantial contributions and are interested in joining the team, reach out on [GitHub Discussions](https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy/discussions).

## Contributors

See the [GitHub contributors page](https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy/graphs/contributors) for the full list of people who have contributed to Nexy.

## Roles

### Maintainer
- Review PRs and triage issues
- Guide project direction and architecture
- Vote on RFCs and breaking changes
- Onboard new contributors

### Contributor
- Submit bug fixes, features, and documentation
- Participate in discussions and code reviews
- Help other community members

## Join the team

The path from contributor to maintainer is based on sustained, high-quality contributions. We look for:

- Consistent, well-tested PRs
- Thoughtful code reviews
- Active participation in discussions
- Understanding of the project's architecture and philosophy

If that sounds like you, keep contributing — we'd love to have you.
